 {
  "h": "17tt5gl",
  "k": "Your Hajj is intact. Arafah, Muzdalifah, the stoning, the trim — all valid without purity. Only tawaf al-ifadah (and the sa'i after it) waits: carry on with every other rite, and after the stoning and the trim on the {1}th stay in the first tahallul; keep up the dhikr and dua from the courtyards, and do ghusl, tawaf and sa'i when you are pure — even on the {2}th or later. Aishah (RA), whose period came before her tawaf, was told: \"Do all that the pilgrims do, except the tawaf of the House until you are pure\" (Bukhari {3}, {4}). <1>The farewell tawaf is waived</1> for you if you are still on your period when you leave (Bukhari {5}). If the group's flight comes before purity, scholars differ — some permit tawaf with precautions in genuine necessity; do not decide alone at the airport: tell your group leader / ask a scholar now, not on the last day.",
  "c": ".acc-b < .acc < .sec-bd",
  "refs": [
   "bukhari:305",
   "bukhari:1755"
  ]
 },
